 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Use the line for the following exercises.\n<br><br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/5f2467ba79e5f18a.png\" alt=\"A line with four points, A, B, C, and D marked on it.\">\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532742,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine <span data-math=\"{\\overline {AB}}  \\cup {\\overline {BD}}\">\\overline {AB}  \\cup \\overline {BD}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You are looking for the union of line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {AB} \"></span> and line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {BD} \"></span>.</p>\n<p>Sketch the two parts separately above the line.</p>\n<p>Union includes all the elements that are in both drawings.</p>\n<p>The union is the line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {AD} \"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\overline {AB}  \\cup \\overline {BD}  = \\overline {AD} \"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{\\overline {AB}}  \\cup {\\overline {BD}}  = \\overline {AD} \">{\\overline {AB}}  \\cup {\\overline {BD}}  = \\overline {AD}</span>. The union of line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {AB} \">\\overline {AB} </span> and the line segment <span data-math=\"{\\overline {BD}}\">{\\overline {BD}}</span> contains all points in each line segment combined."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 532743,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine <span data-math=\"\\overleftarrow {BD}  \\cap {\\overline {BC}} \">\\overleftarrow {BD}  \\cap \\overline {BC} </span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You are looking for the intersection of ray <span data-math=\"\\overleftarrow {BD} \"></span> and line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {BC} \"></span>.</p>\n<p>Sketch the two parts separately above the line.</p>\n<p>Intersection includes only the elements that are common to both drawings.</p>\n<p>The intersection includes only line segment <span data-math=\"\\overline {BC} \"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\overleftarrow {BD}  \\cap \\overline {BC}  = \\overline {BC} \"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\overrightarrow {BD}  \\cap {\\overline {BC}}  = {\\overline {BC}} \">\\overrightarrow {BD}  \\cap \\overline {BC}  = \\overline {BC} </span>. The intersection of the ray <span data-math=\"\\overrightarrow {BD} \">\\overrightarrow {BD} </span> and the line segment <span data-math=\"{\\overline {BC}} \">{\\overline {BC}} </span> contains only the points common to each set, <span data-math=\"{\\overline {BC}} \">\\overline {BC} </span>."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 532744,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine <span data-math=\"\\overleftarrow {BA}  \\cup \\overrightarrow {BD} \">\\overleftarrow {BA}  \\cup \\overrightarrow {BD} </span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\overrightarrow {BA}  \\cup \\overrightarrow {BD}  = \\overleftrightarrow {AD}\">\\overleftarrow {BA}  \\cup \\overrightarrow {BD}  = \\overleftrightarrow {AD}</span>. The union of the ray starting at point <span data-math=\"B\">B</span> and extending infinitely in the direction of <span data-math=\"A\">A</span> and the ray starting at point <span data-math=\"B\">B</span> and extending infinitely in the direction of <span data-math=\"D\">D</span> is the straight line extending infinitely in both directions containing points <span data-math=\"A\">A</span>, <span data-math=\"B\">B</span>, <span data-math=\"C\">C</span>, and <span data-math=\"D\">D</span>."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
